# Sneak names no zone (CR 702.190a: "Any time you could cast an instant during your declare blockers step, you may cast
# this spell by paying [cost] and returning an unblocked creature you control to its owner's hand rather than paying this
# spell's mana cost"), so it is an alternative cost that may be paid whatever zone a rule has the spell cast from (CR
# 118.9, 601.3), unlike warp, which is from the hand only (CR 702.185a). Bot1 casts Shredder's Technique for its mana
# cost on turn 3, destroying one of Bot2's two Ornithopters. On turn 5 Bot1 casts Yawgmoth's Will (Black Lotus) and
# attacks with its Ornithopter; unblocked, in the declare blockers step it casts the Technique from its graveyard for its
# sneak cost {B} (a Swamp), returning the Ornithopter to hand, and destroys Bot2's other Ornithopter. No combat damage is
# dealt; the Technique, leaving the stack, is exiled by the Will, as the Will itself was; the Lotus, sacrificed before
# the Will resolved, stays in the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Shredder's Technique
Black Lotus
Yawgmoth's Will
Swamp
Swamp x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
